{"complete":true,"city":"Rome, Italy","template_id":"global-neighborhoods-one-reason","title":"10 Neighborhoods, One Reason Each","description":"Ten Roman areas, each anchored by one concrete feature—from ancient fragments and industrial structures to garden-city planning and film locations.","icon":"location_city","cards":[{"entity_name":"Monti","title":"Monti","subtitle":"For an unusually dense cross-section of ancient Rome.","notes":"The rione contains the Imperial Fora, Trajan’s Markets, the Domus Aurea and the Ludus Magnus—multiple archaeological layers within one central district.","short_summary":"Imperial sites are threaded through the neighborhood.","source_url":"https://www.turismoroma.it/en/page/rione-i-monti","source_title":"Rione I - Monti","latitude":41.8947077,"longitude":12.4925226,"place_id":"ChIJ5ajmirBhLxMRJC0VLLfKiLE","maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/?q=place_id:ChIJ5ajmirBhLxMRJC0VLLfKiLE"},{"entity_name":"Trastevere","title":"Trastevere","subtitle":"For a Renaissance villa with rooms painted by Raphael and his school.","notes":"Villa Farnesina gives this riverbank rione a focused encounter with Renaissance architecture and fresco painting.","short_summary":"Villa Farnesina places Raphael’s frescoes inside the neighborhood.","source_url":"https://www.turismoroma.it/en/page/rione-xiii-trastevere","source_title":"Rione XIII - Trastevere","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Testaccio","title":"Testaccio","subtitle":"For a hill made from discarded Roman amphora fragments.","notes":"Monte Testaccio, or Monte dei Cocci, accumulated from transport vessels emptied near ancient Rome’s river port.","short_summary":"An ancient ceramic dump became the neighborhood’s defining landform.","source_url":"https://www.turismoroma.it/en/places/monte-dei-cocci","source_title":"Monte dei Cocci","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"EUR","title":"EUR","subtitle":"For a district planned around an exposition that never happened.","notes":"EUR was designed for the 1942 Roman Universal Exposition, canceled after the outbreak of World War II.","short_summary":"A canceled world exposition still shapes the district’s plan.","source_url":"https://www.turismoroma.it/en/quartieri/eur","source_title":"EUR","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Ostiense","title":"Ostiense","subtitle":"For industrial infrastructure reused as part of the contemporary city.","notes":"The former Centrale Montemartini power plant now displays ancient Roman art as a Capitoline Museums venue.","short_summary":"A former power plant now holds classical sculpture.","source_url":"https://www.turismoroma.it/en/quartieri/ostiense-garbatella-spaolo","source_title":"Ostiense - Garbatella - S.Paolo","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Garbatella","title":"Garbatella","subtitle":"For streets and housing laid out on the garden-city model.","notes":"The neighborhood began in the 1920s with worker housing arranged in lots influenced by English garden cities.","short_summary":"Garden-city planning gives the area its small-scale urban form.","source_url":"https://www.turismoroma.it/en/quartieri/ostiense-garbatella-spaolo","source_title":"Ostiense - Garbatella - S.Paolo","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Prati","title":"Prati","subtitle":"For a Roman rione shaped by Piedmontese building styles.","notes":"Its post-unification development produced substantial Umbertine buildings alongside lighter Art Nouveau architecture.","short_summary":"Umbertine and Art Nouveau façades record Rome’s post-unification growth.","source_url":"https://www.turismoroma.it/en/page/rione-xxii-prati","source_title":"Rione XXII - Prati","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"San Lorenzo","title":"San Lorenzo","subtitle":"For a public park dedicated to victims of the 1943 air raids.","notes":"Parco Caduti del 19 Luglio 1943 commemorates the people killed when bombing severely affected the neighborhood.","short_summary":"A neighborhood park holds the memory of the July 1943 bombing.","source_url":"https://www.turismoroma.it/en/places/parco-caduti-del-19-luglio-1943","source_title":"Parco Caduti del 19 Luglio 1943","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Pigneto","title":"Pigneto","subtitle":"For the streets where Pasolini staged much of Accattone.","notes":"The neighborhood’s connection to the 1961 film is still marked by several Pasolini-themed street artworks.","short_summary":"Pasolini’s Accattone remains legible in its streets and murals.","source_url":"https://turismoroma.it/en/itineraries/pasolinis-locations","source_title":"Pasolini's locations","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Rione XVII Sallustiano","title":"Rione XVII Sallustiano","subtitle":"For the ancient garden complex visible below Piazza Sallustio.","notes":"Remains of the Horti Sallustiani survive about 14 metres beneath the modern street level.","short_summary":"Ancient garden architecture sits below the rione’s central square.","source_url":"https://www.turismoroma.it/en/page/rione-xvii-sallustiano","source_title":"Rione XVII - Sallustiano","latitude":41.9071447,"longitude":12.4961067,"place_id":"ChIJL6C3bAhhLxMR9gJKZ7TsSHY","maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/?q=place_id:ChIJL6C3bAhhLxMR9gJKZ7TsSHY"}],"warnings":[]}
